# Control flow and style inside defs. 256x128 artboard, two rows of four 64x64 cells. Outlines come from `style ink`, a 2-wide dark ink stroke.
# Top row, left to right: dots 2 (two red circles of radius 6 side by side, centered on the cell, made by each over 0..n); dots 3 (three of the same circles in a centered row, wider than cell 1);
# dots 3 big:1 (three larger red circles of radius 8 in a centered row, chosen by an if/else on the big parameter; they nearly fill the cell width); ramp_row (four blue circles of radii 3, 5, 7, 9 from a list comprehension, centers at x=200, 214, 228, 242 and y=32, so the row is centered on the cell; centers are 14 apart, so the gaps between neighbors shrink from 6 to 2 and the last two circles overlap by 2; the r9 circle ends at x=251, clear of the artboard edge).
# All top-row circles have the ink outline.
# Bottom row, left to right: a gold square and a blue circle each drawn with `style:ink` (both outlined); the same pair with no style (no outlines, flat fills);
# a group with `style:ink` holding the same gold square and blue circle without style of their own (both outlined, inherited from the group); a group with no style holding the same pair (no outlines).
@artboard 256x128
@target components/control.png

style ink stroke:p.ink,2

def dots n:2 big:0
  let r = if big == 1 then 8 else 6
  let step = r*2+2
  each i in 0..n
    circle r at:(i-(n-1)/2)*step,0 fill:p.red style:ink

def ramp_row n:4
  let radii = [each k in 0..n -> 3+k*2]
  each r in radii
    circle r at:(r-6)*7-3,0 fill:p.blue style:ink

dots 2 at:32,32
dots 3 at:96,32
dots 3 at:160,32 big:1
ramp_row at:224,32
rect 20x20 at:20,96 fill:p.gold style:ink
circle 9 at:44,96 fill:p.blue style:ink
rect 20x20 at:84,96 fill:p.gold
circle 9 at:108,96 fill:p.blue
group at:160,96 style:ink
  rect 20x20 at:-12,0 fill:p.gold
  circle 9 at:12,0 fill:p.blue
group at:224,96
  rect 20x20 at:-12,0 fill:p.gold
  circle 9 at:12,0 fill:p.blue
